{{ 'pdp-brand.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}

{%- comment -%}
  Standalone "Open a claim" page — same functionality as the floating-contact
  widget's Claim tab (3-step wizard -> multipart POST to <endpoint>/claim),
  restyled in the brand's neubrutalist page language (tokens from pdp-brand.css).

  Functionality ported verbatim:
   • Step 1 order number: Next validates against the same /track lookup the
     Track page uses. Definitive "not found" blocks the step and offers the
     message form; network/worker trouble fails OPEN (the claim intake
     re-validates server-side). Last good number is cached.
   • Step 2 issue-type cards set the photo/message requirements; Submit gates
     on them. idempotencyKey stays stable across unchanged retries, rotates on
     any edit. No email field: logged-in customers send the account email
     invisibly; guests are resolved from the order server-side.

  All classes are cp-* and lookups root-scoped, so the floating widget (bb-*)
  coexists untouched. Endpoint: section setting, else the widget's endpoint.
{%- endcomment -%}

<div class="pd">
  <section class="sy-cpage" data-sy-claim-root data-endpoint="{{ section.settings.chat_endpoint | escape }}" data-contact-url="{{ section.settings.contact_url | default: '/pages/contact-us' | escape }}">
    <div class="pd-wrap">
      <div class="cp-hero">
        <span class="pd-eyebrow">{{ section.settings.eyebrow | default: 'Support' }}</span>
        <h1 class="cp-h1">{{ section.settings.heading | default: 'Open a claim' }}</h1>
        <p class="cp-lede">{{ section.settings.lede | default: 'Something wrong with your order? Tell us and we’ll make it right.' }}</p>
      </div>

      <div class="cp-card">
        <div class="cp-dots" aria-hidden="true">
          <span class="cp-dot is-on">1</span><span class="cp-bar"></span><span class="cp-dot">2</span><span class="cp-bar"></span><span class="cp-dot">3</span>
        </div>
        <form class="cp-form" novalidate>
          <div class="cp-step is-active" data-step="1">
            <label class="cp-field">
              <span>Your order number</span>
              <input type="text" class="cp-order" maxlength="100" placeholder="e.g. 154008587601" autocomplete="off" inputmode="numeric" aria-label="Order number">
            </label>
            <button type="button" class="cp-btn cp-next" disabled>Next</button>
          </div>
          <div class="cp-step" data-step="2">
            <div class="cp-q">What went wrong?</div>
            <div class="cp-types">
              <button type="button" class="cp-type" data-type="Damaged in transit" data-photo="1" data-pick="1"><span class="cp-type-ic">📦</span>Damaged in transit</button>
              <button type="button" class="cp-type" data-type="Wrong item" data-photo="1" data-pick="1"><span class="cp-type-ic">🔄</span>Wrong item</button>
              <button type="button" class="cp-type" data-type="Missing item" data-pick="1"><span class="cp-type-ic">📭</span>Missing item</button>
              <button type="button" class="cp-type" data-type="Never received"><span class="cp-type-ic">🕵️</span>Never received</button>
              <button type="button" class="cp-type" data-type="Delayed in transit"><span class="cp-type-ic">⏳</span>Delayed in transit</button>
              <button type="button" class="cp-type cp-type--wide" data-type="Other" data-msg="1"><span class="cp-type-ic">💬</span>Something else</button>
            </div>
            <div class="cp-nav">
              <button type="button" class="cp-back" data-back="1">← Back</button>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="cp-step" data-step="3">
            <div class="cp-picked"></div>
            <div class="cp-field">
              <span>Photos <b class="cp-badge is-opt" data-badge="photo">optional</b></span>
              <label class="cp-drop" for="cp-files-{{ section.id }}">📷 Add photos<input type="file" id="cp-files-{{ section.id }}" class="cp-files cp-vhide" accept="image/*" multiple></label>
            </div>
            <div class="cp-filelist"></div>
            <label class="cp-field">
              <span>Tell us more <b class="cp-badge is-opt" data-badge="msg">optional</b></span>
              <textarea class="cp-msg" rows="4" maxlength="8000" placeholder="Anything that helps us fix this faster…"></textarea>
            </label>
            {%- comment -%} No account email is sent: a logged-in customer can
               claim an order that isn't theirs, so the worker always resolves
               the contact email from the ORDER number instead. {%- endcomment -%}
            <div class="cp-nav">
              <button type="button" class="cp-back" data-back="2">← Back</button>
              <button type="submit" class="cp-btn cp-submit" disabled>{{ section.settings.submit_label | default: 'Submit claim' }}</button>
            </div>
          </div>
          {%- comment -%} Outside the step divs so step-1/2 validation messages
              are visible (and announced) on every step. {%- endcomment -%}
          <div class="cp-status" aria-live="polite"></div>
        </form>
        <div class="cp-done" hidden>
          <div class="cp-done-ic">✓</div>
          <div class="cp-done-h">Claim received</div>
          <p class="cp-done-p"></p>
          <button type="button" class="cp-again">Submit another claim</button>
        </div>
        {%- comment -%} Product picker: shown after choosing a product-related
            issue type — checkboxes for the order's line items (+ Select all).
            The chosen titles ride the claim message as a bullet list. {%- endcomment -%}
        <div class="cp-pick" hidden>
          <div class="cp-pick-card" role="dialog" aria-modal="true">
            <div class="cp-pick-title">Which product is damaged?</div>
            <label class="cp-pick-all"><input type="checkbox" class="cp-pick-allcb"> Select all</label>
            <div class="cp-pick-list"></div>
            <div class="cp-pick-note" hidden>Please pick at least one product.</div>
            <div class="cp-pick-nav">
              <button type="button" class="cp-btn cp-pick-ok">Continue</button>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</div>

<style>
  .sy-cpage{padding:56px 0 88px;background:var(--cream)}
  .sy-cpage .cp-hero{text-align:center;max-width:680px;margin:0 auto 40px}
  .sy-cpage .cp-h1{font-family:var(--display);font-weight:900;font-size:clamp(34px,6vw,60px);line-height:.95;letter-spacing:-.01em;text-transform:uppercase;margin:18px 0 12px;text-wrap:balance}
  .sy-cpage .cp-lede{font-family:var(--serif);font-size:clamp(15px,1.5vw,17.5px);line-height:1.55;color:var(--ink-2);margin:0 auto;max-width:48ch}

  .sy-cpage .cp-card{position:relative;max-width:640px;margin:0 auto;background:var(--paper);border:var(--rule-2);border-radius:var(--r-card);box-shadow:6px 6px 0 var(--ink);padding:28px;font-family:var(--serif)}
